#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166501 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d3cb2fcb-3457-5a89-8968-6c0f2c2cfa83" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Product of Cosines"}] :question/id #uuid "177a0110-424b-5ac3-a24e-e817cbcf479c" :question/math-academy-id "e-21823" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral $\\displaystyle \\int_{\\pi/4}^{\\pi/2} \\cos(9x)\\cos(x)\\,\\text{d}x$." :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the sum and difference formulas for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\cos (α - β) &= \\cos α\\cos β + \\sin α\\sin β \\\\\n\\cos (α + β) &= \\cos α\\cos β - \\sin α\\sin β\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding these equations, we get the following product-to-sum identity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\cos (α - β) + \\cos (α + β) &= 2\\cos α\\cos β \\\\\n\\cos α\\cos β &= \\frac{1}{2}(\\cos (α - β) + \\cos (α + β))\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\cos (9x)\\cos (x) &= \\frac{1}{2}(\\cos (9x - x) + \\cos (9x + x)) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}(\\cos (8x) + \\cos (10x))\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the integral gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int_{π/4}^{π/2}\\cos (9x)\\cos (x)dx &= \\int_{π/4}^{π/2}\\frac{1}{2}\\cos (8x) + \\frac{1}{2}\\cos (10x)dx \\\\\n&= [\\frac{1}{16}\\sin (8x) + \\frac{1}{20}\\sin (10x)]_{π/4}^{π/2} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{16}(\\sin (4π) - \\sin (2π)) + \\frac{1}{20}(\\sin (5π) - \\sin (\\frac{5π}{2})) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{16}(0 - 0) + \\frac{1}{20}(0 - 1) \\\\\n&=-\\frac{1}{20}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166502 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8a371de4-7c3f-5687-bd3a-d3ab5ab803ce" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Product of Sines"}] :question/id #uuid "ebf57ac7-29e3-595e-8a72-032e10c470aa" :question/math-academy-id "e-21824" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral $\\displaystyle \\int \\sin(12x)\\sin(5x)\\,\\text{d}x$." :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the sum and difference formulas for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\cos (α - β) &= \\cos α\\cos β + \\sin α\\sin β \\\\\n\\cos (α + β) &= \\cos α\\cos β - \\sin α\\sin β\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubtracting the second equation from the first, we get the following product-to-sum identity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\cos (α - β) - \\cos (α + β) &= 2\\sin α\\sin β \\\\\n\\sin α\\sin β &= \\frac{1}{2}(\\cos (α - β) - \\cos (α + β))\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\sin (12x)\\sin (5x) &= \\frac{1}{2}(\\cos (12x - 5x) - \\cos (12x + 5x)) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}(\\cos (7x) - \\cos (17x))\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the integral gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int\\sin (12x)\\sin (5x)dx &= \\int\\frac{1}{2}\\cos (7x) - \\frac{1}{2}\\cos (17x)dx \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{14}\\sin (7x) - \\frac{1}{34}\\sin (17x) + C\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an arbitrary constant."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166503 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9d3b7f35-fcd1-5443-b0ea-0b06e016e0c3" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Product of Sine and Cosine"}] :question/id #uuid "14466847-40e1-5a4f-b50a-23b62590f0a2" :question/math-academy-id "e-21825" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral $\\displaystyle \\int_{0}^{\\pi/2} \\sin(2x)\\cos(4x)\\,\\text{d}x$." :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the sum and difference formulas for sine:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\sin (α + β) &= \\sin α\\cos β + \\cos α\\sin β \\\\\n\\sin (α - β) &= \\sin α\\cos β - \\cos α\\sin β\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding these equations, we get the following product-to-sum identity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\sin (α + β) + \\sin (α - β) &= 2\\sin α\\cos β \\\\\n\\sin α\\cos β &= \\frac{1}{2}(\\sin (α + β) + \\sin (α - β))\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\sin (2x)\\cos (4x) &= \\frac{1}{2}(\\sin (2x + 4x) + \\sin (2x - 4x)) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}(\\sin (6x) + \\sin (-2x)) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}(\\sin (6x) - \\sin (2x))\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the integral gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int_{0}^{π/2}\\sin (2x)\\cos (4x)dx &= \\int_{0}^{π/2}\\frac{1}{2}\\sin (6x) - \\frac{1}{2}\\sin (2x)dx \\\\\n&= [- \\frac{1}{12}\\cos (6x) + \\frac{1}{4}\\cos (2x)]_{0}^{π/2} \\\\\n&=-\\frac{1}{12}(\\cos (3π) - \\cos (0)) + \\frac{1}{4}(\\cos (π) - \\cos (0)) \\\\\n&=-\\frac{1}{12}(-1 - 1) + \\frac{1}{4}(-1 - 1) \\\\\n&=-\\frac{1}{3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167216 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8a371de4-7c3f-5687-bd3a-d3ab5ab803ce" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Product of Sines"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c202af47-5cc0-5423-9bc1-f59200a5ab79" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}\\sin (4x) - \\frac{1}{12}\\sin (6x) + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164855} {:answer/id #uuid "e15fb7b1-c405-521a-9c0c-d940a9b38c6c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sin (x) - \\frac{1}{5}\\sin (5x) + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164856} {:answer/id #uuid "17be339b-6d42-52da-91f6-0ca19e3be727" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}\\sin (4x) - \\frac{1}{10}\\sin (5x) + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164857} {:answer/id #uuid "4f3eea91-be34-59c3-a8ca-309b6f31b2f1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}\\sin (x) + \\frac{1}{6}\\sin (3x) + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164858} {:answer/id #uuid "5814c881-6d20-56dc-b07c-808e1798e80d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}\\cos (4x) - \\frac{1}{12}\\cos (3x) + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164859}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c202af47-5cc0-5423-9bc1-f59200a5ab79" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}\\sin (4x) - \\frac{1}{12}\\sin (6x) + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164855} :answer-field/id #uuid "8154c11c-70fc-56de-8735-13730e5f9f4b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type